{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1788200643,"nonce":"YeEQsz02FWzr9qiUQ0RvSrvxkSw=","target":"fbb2c59233a787bbacecf4f8a1fb07c6cd885c60543e09503630f50370d64d49","message":"Orchestration run ledger. Session 9, dorian's Linux box, 2026-08-31.\nBody = current state (edited in place). Comments = events.\n\n## Goal\n\nGet 4.1 (96d9315) fully unblocked, and end the machine-exclusivity of 2.5 by\nvendoring baseviz.\n\n## Plan (verbatim)\n\nA — 2.5 PNG render channel (f7b6207, agent:opus, p2, wave:2). Includes\nVENDORING baseviz into this repo. Rationale: rimworld-tools has git but NO\nREMOTE, so baseviz has never left this disk — that unpushed dependency is the\nentire reason 2.5 is dorian's-box-only. The issue's own comment #2 (Evan,\nsession 3) already resolved import-vs-vendor toward vendoring: \"an unversioned\ndependency cannot be pinned.\" Vendor target is ~40KB of python: canvas.py,\ncatalog.py, ir.py, __main__.py, server.py, plus BaseVizCatalogDumper (184K, mod\nwith source) which is what makes the catalog mod-aware. Touches: rwa/, new\nvendored baseviz/, one new `map dump` verb in Source/.\n\nB — 4087644 Job-ordering verbs report success for orders that did nothing\n(agent:opus, p1, wave:3). TryTakeOrderedJob early-returns true when\ncurJob.JobIsSameAs, so all 17 job verbs report accepted:1 for calls that changed\nnothing. Blocks an honest 4.1: 4.1 defines checklist items that must \"always\nproduce either ok or an action\", so a lying verb surface bakes false ok's into\nthe playbook and surfaces in 4.3's demo. Touches: PawnActs.cs, PawnSerializer.cs.\n\nC — 2f2796e Verify the issue backlog before building to it (agent:opus, p1,\nwave:0). Verification pass over open issues, four verdicts (CONFIRMED /\nCORRECTED / UNVERIFIABLE FROM SOURCE / INFERENCE, UNMARKED). Read-only, no\nbuild, no bench, git-bug comments only — touches NO files.\n\nRound 2 after this: 4.1 (96d9315) as agent:fable per the muster's resolution\ncomment (Evan, 2026-08-31: the fable labels stand on this box).\n\n## Lanes\n\nSmall (orchestrator subagents): C — 2f2796e\nBig (worker sessions): W1: f7b6207 (A) · W2: 4087644 (B)\n\nA and B are independent, not sequenced. Both slots live at once.\n\n## State\n\n| issue   | lane  | status   | branch                              | note |\n|---------|-------|----------|-------------------------------------|------|\n| f7b6207 | big   | vetting  | worktree-issue-f7b6207-png-render   | W1 = autorimmer-27, ff-merged to b70a9e7 |\n| 4087644 | big   | vetting  | worktree-issue-4087644              | W2 = autorimmer-41, ff-merged to b70a9e7 |\n| 2f2796e | small | building | (subagent worktree)                 | C — read-only, git-bug comments only |\n\nstatuses: queued · vetting · cleared · building · ready · merged · closed · parked\n\n## Comms\n\nOrchestrator: autorimmer-62 (G1). W1: autorimmer-27. W2: autorimmer-41.\nBoth workers pinned the orchestrator and exchanged NOT-ORCHESTRATOR with each\nother, then compared territories independently and agreed disjoint.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- **Territories.** W1 owns `rwa/`, the new vendored `baseviz/`, and its ONE new\n  verb file in `Source/AutoRimmer/`. W2 owns `PawnActs.cs` and\n  `PawnSerializer.cs`. C owns no files at all.\n- **Every worker gets its own git worktree.** Disjoint files are not enough; a\n  shared HEAD is the hazard (session 4).\n- **Workers never launch RimWorld.** The orchestrator runs all in-game\n  acceptance personally. `_RimWorld-Agent` is the only install anyone may ever\n  launch, and only the orchestrator launches it.\n- **No worker builds before GO.** Vet first: `VET \u003cid\u003e: CONFIRM | AMEND |\n  BLOCK` with evidence.\n- **Observers never mutate game state.** PawnSafe.cs / WorldSafe.cs hold the\n  guarded routes.\n- **The gate lives in the widget.** Every player verb re-implements its\n  precondition and cites it (file + member). `dev:*` may bypass.\n- C must NOT verify f7b6207 or 4087644 — their own workers vet those. C covers\n  the rest of the open backlog, `state:next` before `backlog`.\n\n## Seams raised and resolved (both dissolved, neither is a conflict risk)\n\nW1 named two places the two workers might collide. Both were read at the\nsource and neither exists:\n\n1. **`AutoRimmer.csproj` does not enumerate `.cs`.** Line 7 sets\n   `\u003cEnableDefaultCompileItems\u003etrue\u003c/EnableDefaultCompileItems\u003e`, so it globs.\n   A new source file needs no csproj edit. Only a new PackageReference or\n   managed Reference would touch that file, and the orchestrator is to be told\n   first if one is needed.\n2. **The verb registry has no central list.** `VerbRegistry.RegisterAll()`\n   reflects over `typeof(VerbRegistry).Assembly.GetTypes()` for `[Verb]` static\n   methods of shape `static object M(VerbContext)`. A verb registers itself by\n   carrying the attribute — no array, no switch, no file to append to. The two\n   workers cannot collide there even in principle.\n\nFalling out of the same read, and told to W1: a malformed handler does NOT fail\nthe build. Wrong signature or a duplicate op string produces a startup\n`Log.Warning` and the verb is silently skipped, surfacing only as unknown-verb\nat the call site. `Log.Warning` is not a red error, so a skipped verb does not\ntrip the zero-red-errors invariant and is genuinely quiet.\n\n## Source reads the orchestrator has already done (workers told not to re-derive)\n\n**`TryTakeOrderedJob`'s early-out is CONFIRMED and it is UNCONDITIONAL.**\n`Verse.AI/Pawn_JobTracker.cs`:\n\n    job.playerForced = true;\n    if (curJob != null \u0026\u0026 curJob.JobIsSameAs(pawn, job)) { return true; }\n    ...\n    isDownEvent = isDownEvent || requestQueueing;\n\n`requestQueueing` is not read until after the return, so the collision fires\nwhether or not the caller asked to queue. W2 raised this as an open question —\nwhether the `already-doing-it` pre-check must be conditional on the queue flag.\nIt must not be. **The queued case is worse than the base case:** with\n`queue:true` the caller explicitly asked to enqueue, and on a current-job\ncollision nothing is enqueued at all — no queue entry, no current-job change,\nno trace — so the agent gains a queued action that does not exist. Note\n`JobIsSameAs` compares against `curJob` only, never against the existing queue.\n\nThis also sharpens fix #3 (publish `pawn.jobs.AllJobs()`): the body's rationale\nis that `queue:true` makes the ordered job invisible because `job_def` names the\ncurrent job. True, but the sharper case is that the ordered job is invisible\nbecause it was never created. Queue publication does not rescue that; only the\npre-check does.\n\n## Bench and build facts (session 9, this box)\n\n- Build: `dotnet build -c Release` from `Source/AutoRimmer/`, NOT the repo root.\n- Step 0 paid: `b70a9e7` fixed AutoRimmer.csproj, whose \"machine-portable\"\n  fallback had no Linux line. A bare build here produced 630 CS0246 errors that\n  read as a broken source tree. A bare `dotnet build -c Release` now works on\n  both benches; RIMWORLD_MANAGED still wins where set.\n- **`cmp -l` across machines is a trap.** A Linux build at the same commit\n  differs from the shipped BORGES blob by 185,249 bytes at identical file size —\n  the pdb path length shifts the tail and cascades. The workspace CLAUDE.md's\n  \"under ~200 differing bytes means the IL is unchanged\" rule is PER MACHINE\n  ONLY.\n- **No pwsh on this box.** `accept/32b9e01-orders-makingfor.ps1` cannot run\n  here. `accept/3.4-pawn-orders.py` is the python twin and does run. Three\n  acceptance notes have no driver in any language: `auto-arm-lever.md`,\n  `1eb2262-stable-pawn-order.md`, `manual-work-priorities.md`.\n- Bench is `autostart.rws` at tick 89426 — the session-7 colony, NOT the\n  3-colonist quicktest map at tick 607 that every session 7–8 \"verified on the\n  bench\" claim refers to. Prefs 2560x1600 fullscreen, devMode on.\n\n## Not in this round\n\n- Orchestrator debt, three sessions old: factor the four private `Act` emitters\n  (AreaVerbs, DesignationVerbs, ZoneVerbs, PawnActs) into one helper; fold\n  `Pawn_ReadingTracker` into `PawnSafe.Policies`.\n- `70ac258` things ordering (ports mechanically from 1eb2262).\n- `0d9cbd7` world-fixture steps do not chain.\n- Acceptance portability: the three driverless notes, and 32b9e01's pwsh-only\n  driver.\n\n## Lineage\n\nG1 — active, merges: 0","files":null}]}